<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruaidrí Mac Duinn Sléibe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1201</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ruaidrí Mac Duinn Sléibe was the last powerful king of Ulaid, the over-kingdom of eastern Ulster, and head of the Dál Fiatach. In 1177 the Anglo-Norman adventurer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-de-courcy">John de Courcy</a> invaded and defeated him near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/downpatrick">Downpatrick</a>, and despite repeated attempts he could not recover his kingdom, which became the Earldom of Ulster.</p></div>
